      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Alterations, either an increase or decrease, in the distal flow velocity over time are associated with alterations in vessel diameter and/or unstable flow velocity. Unexplained unstable flow velocity patterns should act as early warning signs to prompt the interventionalist to assess continued coronary patency and need for renewed interventions."},
